## Interface: 120100, 50504, 40402, 30405, 20506, 11509
## Title: Combat Analyzer
## Notes: Combat performance analyzer (Retail + Classic)
## Author: OpenAI
## Version: 0.1.0
## SavedVariables: CombatAnalyzerDB

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Interface: comma-delimited list so a single TOC covers every currently
# live client flavor without needing separate _Mainline / _Classic TOC files:
#   120100 -> Retail / Mainline
#    50504 -> Classic Progression (Mists of Pandaria Classic)
#    40402 -> Classic Progression (Cataclysm Classic, still installed by some users)
#    30405 -> Classic Progression (Wrath Classic / Titan Reforged)
#    20506 -> Classic Progression (Burning Crusade Classic)
#    11509 -> Classic Era (Vanilla)
# Update these numbers as Blizzard ships new patches; an outdated number only
# triggers the cosmetic "out of date" flag, it never blocks loading.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Shared core: version detection, data model, combat lifecycle, slash commands.
Core.lua

# Shared combat-log normalization/dispatch layer (client-agnostic).
CombatLog.lua

# Data-acquisition layer: exactly one of these two loads, chosen by the
# client itself via the AllowLoadGameType conditional directive. Neither
# file is even parsed on the "wrong" client, so we never risk registering
# an event or calling an API that doesn't exist there.
CombatLog_Retail.lua [AllowLoadGameType mainline]
CombatLog_Classic.lua [AllowLoadGameType classic]

# Analysis modules: operate only on the normalized structure produced above,
# so none of them need to know whether they're running on Retail or Classic.
Damage.lua
Buffs.lua
Interrupts.lua
Deaths.lua
Timeline.lua
UI.lua
